    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the single test class `AcceptanceTest` passing). AuditLogCapture and AcceptanceBase are support classes, not test classes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag on the owner response.\n\n**Change:** When more than 80 owners already carry today's business-day registration date, responses now include `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\n**Files modified:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean read-only property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time, giving `OwnerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(...)`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant.\n   - Added `isBulkSignupWarningActive()`, which counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today's business day (the same accumulation basis the existing per-day create limit uses) and returns `count > 80`.\n   - Set the flag on the DTO in both `addOwner` (the create response) and `getOwner` (the read path the acceptance test asserts against).\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold`) creates a fresh owner and reads back `$.bulkSignupWarning == false`, which passes since the count stays well under the threshold. The `> 80` branch reuses the same daily-accumulation path as the existing daily-limit rule.",
